What:		/sys/class/drm/card[0-9]/crtc-[0-9]/errors/frame_start_timeout
Date:		January 2026
Contact:	Ken Huang <kenbshuang@google.com>
Description:
		A read-only file that contains the number of times a frame
		start interrupt has timed out. A frame start timeout
		indicates that the DPU failed to start processing a new
		frame within the expected timeframe.

What:		/sys/class/drm/card[0-9]/crtc-[0-9]/errors/frame_start_missing
Date:		January 2026
Contact:	Ken Huang <kenbshuang@google.com>
Description:
		A read-only file that contains the number of times a frame
		start interrupt was missed. This can happen if the system is
		heavily loaded and the interrupt handler is not scheduled in
		time.

What:		/sys/class/drm/card[0-9]/crtc-[0-9]/errors/frame_done_timeout
Date:		January 2026
Contact:	Ken Huang <kenbshuang@google.com>
Description:
		A read-only file that contains the number of times a frame
		done interrupt has timed out. A frame done timeout
		indicates that the DPU failed to finish processing a
		frame within the expected timeframe.

What:		/sys/class/drm/card[0-9]/crtc-[0-9]/errors/frame_done_missing
Date:		January 2026
Contact:	Ken Huang <kenbshuang@google.com>
Description:
		A read-only file that contains the number of times a frame
		done interrupt was missed. This can happen if the system is
		heavily loaded and the interrupt handler is not scheduled in
		time.

What:		/sys/class/drm/card[0-9]/crtc-[0-9]/errors/underrun_count
Date:		January 2026
Contact:	Ken Huang <kenbshuang@google.com>
Description:
		A read-only file that contains the number of times the DPU
		has experienced an underrun. An underrun occurs when the
		DPU runs out of data to process, which can lead to visual
		artifacts on the display.

What:		/sys/class/drm/card[0-9]/crtc-[0-9]/recovery_stats/<source>_success
What:		/sys/class/drm/card[0-9]/crtc-[0-9]/recovery_stats/<source>_failure
What:		/sys/class/drm/card[0-9]/crtc-[0-9]/recovery_stats/<source>_max_retry
Date:		January 2026
Contact:	Ken Lin <lyenting@google.com>
Description:
		Read-only files containing statistics for display recovery attempts,
		grouped by their trigger source (manual, frame_update_timeout, dsi_err, ddic_err).

		- success: Count of successful recovery attempts where the display stack
		  suspended and resumed without error.
		- failure: Count of failed recovery attempts where the suspend/resume
		  sequence encountered an error.
		- max_retry: Count of times the recovery mechanism reached its maximum
		  consecutive attempt limit.
